.\" man/man3/TreeSitter::Node.3cr
.\" Generated by scripts/man.cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "TreeSitter::Node" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "treesitter 0.1.0" "treesitter API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
TreeSitter::Node \- A node of a \fB\%Tree\fR: its type, byte range, points and neighbors.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "treesitter"\fR
.sp
\fBstruct TreeSitter::Node\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
A node of a \fB\%Tree\fR: its type, byte range, points and neighbors. Navigation returns \fB\%nil\fR where there is no node.
A node is a value; it stays valid while its tree is not edited.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef ==(other : Node) : Bool\fR
Whether \fIother\fR is the same node.
.TP 4
\fBdef child(index : Int32) : Node | Nil\fR
The child at \fIindex\fR, anonymous ones included.
.TP 4
\fBdef child_count : Int32\fR
Number of children, anonymous ones included.
.TP 4
\fBdef descendant(from : Int32, to : Int32) : Node | Nil\fR
The smallest node within this one that spans the bytes \fIfrom\fR...\fIto\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef end_byte : Int32\fR
Byte offset where the node ends (exclusive).
.TP 4
\fBdef end_point : Point\fR
Where the node ends.
.TP 4
\fBdef error? : Bool\fR
Whether this node is an \fB\%ERROR\fR node, text the parser could not fit.
.TP 4
\fBdef extra? : Bool\fR
Whether this node is extra, such as a comment, which may appear anywhere.
.TP 4
\fBdef field(name : String) : Node | Nil\fR
The child in the grammar field \fIname\fR (\fB\%"key"\fR, \fB\%"body"\fR).
.TP 4
\fBdef has_error? : Bool\fR
Whether this node is or contains an error or a missing node.
.TP 4
\fBdef missing? : Bool\fR
Whether the parser inserted this zero\-width node to recover from an error.
.TP 4
\fBdef named? : Bool\fR
Whether the grammar names this node (rules, not anonymous tokens such as \fB\%","\fR).
.TP 4
\fBdef named_child(index : Int32) : Node | Nil\fR
The named child at \fIindex\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef named_child_count : Int32\fR
Number of named children.
.TP 4
\fBdef named_descendant(from : Int32, to : Int32) : Node | Nil\fR
The smallest named node within this one that spans the bytes \fIfrom\fR...\fIto\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef next_named_sibling : Node | Nil\fR
The next named sibling.
.TP 4
\fBdef next_sibling : Node | Nil\fR
The next sibling, anonymous ones included.
.TP 4
\fBdef parent : Node | Nil\fR
The enclosing node, \fB\%nil\fR for the root.
.TP 4
\fBdef previous_named_sibling : Node | Nil\fR
The previous named sibling.
.TP 4
\fBdef previous_sibling : Node | Nil\fR
The previous sibling, anonymous ones included.
.TP 4
\fBdef range : Range(Int32, Int32)\fR
The node\(aqs bytes as an exclusive range.
.TP 4
\fBdef region : Region\fR
The node\(aqs bytes and points as a \fB\%Region\fR, for \fB\%Parser#included_regions=\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef start_byte : Int32\fR
Byte offset where the node starts.
.TP 4
\fBdef start_point : Point\fR
Where the node starts.
.TP 4
\fBdef tree : Tree\fR
The tree this node belongs to.
.TP 4
\fBdef type : String\fR
The grammar\(aqs name for this kind of node (\fB\%"pair"\fR, \fB\%","\fR, \fB\%"ERROR"\fR).
